What is Online Gaming?
Online gaming encompasses any video game experience that relies on a persistent internet connection for gameplay, matchmaking, social interaction, or content delivery. Unlike traditional cartridge or disc based titles, online games can be updated dynamically, support real time data exchange, and enable large global communities. This connectivity paradigm has unlocked new revenue models such as subscription services, battle pass monetisation, and in game advertising, which collectively underpin the market’s valuation.
